Source: pxf
Maintainer: Greengage <greengage@greengagedb.org>
Section: database
Build-Depends: debhelper (>= 13),
	 lsb-release

Package: pxf-server
Priority: optional
Architecture: amd64
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}
Description: PXF core service
	The pxf-server package provides the core PXF service and plugins.
	This package includes the PXF Java service, Tomcat runtime, and all built-in
	connectors required to query external data sources.
	PXF is a query federation engine that accesses data residing in external
	systems such as Hadoop, Hive, HBase, S3, Google Cloud Storage,
	relational databases, among other external systems.

Package: pxf-cli
Priority: optional
Architecture: amd64
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends},
	 pxf-server
Description: PXF CLI Utility
	The pxf-cli package provides the pxf command-line utility for managing
	the PXF service and configuration on Greengage hosts.
	The pxf-cli utility allows you to start, stop, and manage PXF instances,
	synchronize configurations across the cluster, perform other tasks.
	PXF is a query federation engine that accesses data residing in external
	systems such as Hadoop, Hive, HBase, S3, Google Cloud Storage,
	relational databases, among other external systems.

Package: greengage@GP_MAJORVERSION@-pxf-fdw
Priority: optional
Architecture: amd64
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends},
	 greengage@GP_MAJORVERSION@
Provides: pxf-fdw
Description: PXF Foreign Data Wrapper for Greengage@GP_MAJORVERSION@
	The greengage@GP_MAJORVERSION@-pxf-fdw package provides the Greengage@GP_MAJORVERSION@ extension that
	implements a Foreign Data Wrapper (FDW) for PXF.
	PXF is a query federation engine that accesses data residing in external
	systems such as Hadoop, Hive, HBase, S3, Google Cloud Storage,
	relational databases, among other external systems.
